"""Tavish Gray, part A: biography (Origins, Red Dead Redemption 2 chapter 3, his death and the Edinburgh letter,
the 1907 epilogue).

SOURCE REGISTER (fetched Oct 2026; local copies in scripts/v3/work/tavish/ and scripts/v3/work/_m/):
- Red Dead Wiki EN character page "Tavish Gray" (en.txt) and FR page (fr.txt).
- Red Dead Wiki mission page "Horse Flesh for Dinner" (story, trivia: dialogue variants before/after "The Fine Joys of
  Tobacco", optional greet/antagonize exchange, mission failure). No "/dialogues" page exists for it (Oct 2026).
- Red Dead Wiki pages "Gray Family" (1755 emigration, 1806 Lucille/Douglas story, Joe Butler, members, 1907),
  "Caliga Hall" (slave labor, tobacco and cotton, decline after abolition, east porch, 1907), "Gray's Secret" (point of
  interest; available after "Horse Flesh for Dinner"; body unchanged in 1907), "Gray Family History Letter" (full text of
  the letter), "Leigh Gray", "Beau Gray", "Jock Gray", "A Short Walk in a Pretty Town" (deaths).
- Screenshots on the Red Dead Wiki ("RDR2_POI_18_Gray's Secret_01.png", "Gray's secet.jpeg"), looked at directly
  (copies in scripts/v3/work/tavish/fc/img_*.jpg): the body sits slumped in a wicker chair, right hand on the left forearm,
  beside a small marble table holding a coffee pot and a cup. No weapon, no wound, no blood visible.
- TRANSCRIPT: "Red Dead Redemption 2 Full Transcript", Game Scripts Wiki
  (game-scripts-wiki.blogspot.com/2022/01/red-dead-redemption-2.html), fan transcript of the cutscenes, saved as
  scripts/v3/work/tavish/fc/gsw.txt (gitignored). Scenes read in full: "The New South" (Archibald on the Grays, Caliga
  Hall, the Parlor House), "American Distillation" (Archibald on the old fortune), "The Course of True Love I + II" (guards
  at Caliga Hall, Beau's self-introduction), "Advertising, The New American Art" (Dutch: "Sheriff Gray kindly put in a word
  with his father"), "Horse Flesh for Dinner" (the whole Tavish scene, the ride, Clay Davies, Arthur's journal), "The Fine
  Joys of Tobacco" (Sean on security doubled, Hamish on "Mr. Gray"), "A Short Walk in a Pretty Town" (Micah: the Grays
  spoke to Bill; Bill: they think it was the Braithwaites; Sheriff Gray's lines; Jock), "Blood Feuds, Ancient and Modern"
  (opening).
- Consistency: fact-checked parts catherine_A/B/C, arthur_B/D, javier_A/B/C, john_A, hosea_B, micah_B, sean_B;
  HOUSE_FACTS (Leigh Gray deputizes Dutch, Arthur and Bill to shut down a Braithwaite still; "A Short Walk in a Pretty
  Town": Sean killed, shooter not named, Sheriff Leigh Gray dies, never "the Grays are wiped out").

Verified in the transcript: Beau calls himself the son of Tavish, nephew of Sheriff Leigh Gray and grandson of Murdo
Gray, and mentions his brothers; Tavish speaks of his sons (plural); Arthur says he has met Tavish's "son, the sheriff"
and nobody corrects him (John cuts in); Dutch says the sheriff put in a word with "his father"; Tavish says the
Braithwaites killed his uncle, that the Grays cannot be seen to get too close, that they have gold, that the horses will
fetch five thousand and that the Clemens Cove buyer pays fifty cents on the dollar; John calls him a crazy old fool on
the way out; Clay Davies offers 650, then pays 700; in the transcript version Tavish raises no suspicion about the fields
(it is the version played before "The Fine Joys of Tobacco"). Tavish does not appear in "A Short Walk in a Pretty Town".
WIKI-ONLY, attributed in the text: "patriarch and eldest member"; Caliga Hall built on slave labor, tobacco and cotton,
decline after abolition; the 1755/1806 family history; Joe Butler's claims; the post-tobacco dialogue variant and the
optional greet/antagonize exchange; the body being available after "Horse Flesh for Dinner" (POI page) versus "after the
battle" (character page); the body unchanged in 1907; Caliga Hall still run by the family in 1907; Harmon Thomas.
Ownership: Tavish's own lines are paraphrased here (part B "In his own words" may quote his war/Scottish family lines,
part C quotes his job lines); Dutch's "put in a word with his father", Beau's self-introduction, Clay Davies, John on the
five thousand, Arthur's and John's journal entries = part C Quotes. Letter: told HERE only, partly quoted verbatim.
John's real-surname slip, the mission-failure rule, the Moffat surname and the "only POI tied to a mission" = part C Trivia.

Excluded: the cause of death (character page: "possibly suicide, more likely a heart attack judging by the state of his
corpse"; Gray's Secret, Caliga Hall, Gray Family and the FR wiki: suicide; the game shows neither: only the body is
described); "Tavish and Leigh plot revenge" (FR wiki; not shown, Tavish is absent from the ambush); "the Grays plot revenge
and offer the job" with Tavish behind it (no scene; Micah says only that the Grays spoke to Bill); "most of the Gray family
is killed" / "all the Grays killed except Tavish" (HOUSE: never "wiped out"; only Leigh Gray, Jock Gray, Archibald and
gunmen are shown dying); the identity of "Old Man Gray" in Sean's line (could be Tavish, not stated: the line is
paraphrased without a name); the wiki's reading that the gang "received false information" (speculation); the "No true
Scotsman" reading of the letter (wiki analysis); Beau's "my uncle used to keep his own half-brother as a slave" (uncle not
named: could be Leigh or another relative); Hamish's killer (transcript: Arthur; wiki: Arthur or Sean; not about Tavish).

FIX PASS (22 Oct 2026, after fc_report1/2 + coverage_report): added from the transcript (gsw.txt) Tavish's suspicion of the
newcomers ("Who are you?", "Sure... and bad men"), Trelawny on "rebel gold and... marrying cousins" (The New South), the
stable hand naming Cerberus, Old Faithful and Old Father Time, Arthur's "We just robbed their horses too" (Fine Joys), Sadie's
1907 line ("A Quick Favor for an Old Friend": "since the time of the Grays and Braithwaites"). Wiki-only, attributed: French
period of Scarlett Meadows (Gray Family page), Douglas Gray as an ancestor, Jock Gray as a relative, back porch, Arthur
revealing the fire on the ride out (Horse Flesh mission page). Pearson's 1907 line attributed to the wiki quote list (as in
simon_C). Pot described as "metal pot" (nothing marks it as coffee). Dutch's rob-both plan placed in "Advertising, The New
American Art". The 1907 state of Caliga Hall stays HERE (Caliga Hall section points to it). "Scot in exile" quoted in B
Names only; the uncle line is told once here (Horse Flesh paragraph) and quoted in C.
"""


def two(en, fr): return {"en": en, "fr": fr}


BLOCKS = [
    # ================================================================ Origins
    {"h3": two("Origins", "Origines"), "year": ""},
    {"p": two("The game gives no date or place of birth for Tavish Gray. In 1899 he heads the Gray family, the owners of Caliga Hall, a tobacco plantation in Bayou Nwa, in the state of Lemoyne, between Rhodes and Saint Denis. The Red Dead Wiki describes him as the family's patriarch and its eldest member. His son Beau Gray introduces himself to Arthur as the son of Tavish, the nephew of Sheriff Leigh Gray and the grandson of Murdo Gray. This makes Tavish the brother of the sheriff and the son of Murdo. Tavish speaks of his sons in the plural, and Beau mentions his brothers, but Beau is the only son named.",
              "Le jeu ne donne ni la date ni le lieu de naissance de Tavish Gray. En 1899, il est à la tête de la famille Gray, propriétaire de Caliga Hall, une plantation de tabac du Bayou Nwa, dans l'État du Lemoyne, entre Rhodes et Saint-Denis. Le Red Dead Wiki le présente comme le patriarche de la famille et son doyen. Son fils Beau Gray se présente à Arthur comme le fils de Tavish, le neveu du shérif Leigh Gray et le petit-fils de Murdo Gray. Tavish est donc le frère du shérif et le fils de Murdo. Il parle de ses fils au pluriel, et Beau évoque ses frères, mais Beau est le seul dont le nom soit donné.")},
    {"p": two("The game is not consistent on this point. When Arthur meets Tavish, he says he has met his son, the sheriff, and nobody corrects him. Earlier, Dutch explains that Sheriff Gray got the gang its meeting at Caliga Hall by putting in a word with his father (see Quotes). The Red Dead Wiki records both versions and treats the mismatch as an inconsistency in the game. Beau's version, which also appears on the wiki's family pages, is the one this profile follows.",
              "Le jeu se contredit sur ce point. Lors de sa rencontre avec Tavish, Arthur dit avoir fait la connaissance de son fils, le shérif, et personne ne le reprend. Plus tôt, Dutch explique que si la bande a obtenu son rendez-vous à Caliga Hall, c'est parce que le shérif Gray en a touché un mot à son père (voir Citations). Le Red Dead Wiki relève les deux versions et y voit une incohérence du jeu. Cette fiche retient celle de Beau, qui est aussi celle des pages consacrées à la famille sur le wiki.")},
    {"p": two("Tavish presents the Grays as an old Scottish family (see In his own words). The Rhodes deputy Archibald MacGregor tells Arthur that the Grays have lived at Caliga Hall for generations and own all the businesses in Rhodes, including the saloon. The family also holds the law in town through Sheriff Leigh Gray. The Red Dead Wiki gives more background. The family arrived in Scarlett Meadows when the region still belonged to France. Its wealth came from tobacco and cotton worked by slaves before the Civil War. Once slavery was abolished, that wealth shrank.",
              "Tavish présente les Gray comme une vieille famille écossaise (voir Dans ses propres mots). Archibald MacGregor, l'adjoint du shérif de Rhodes, raconte à Arthur que les Gray vivent à Caliga Hall depuis des générations et possèdent tous les commerces de Rhodes, saloon compris. La famille tient aussi la loi en ville, par l'intermédiaire du shérif Leigh Gray. Le Red Dead Wiki en dit davantage. La famille s'est établie dans les Scarlett Meadows à l'époque où la région était encore française. Avant la guerre de Sécession, sa richesse reposait sur le tabac et le coton, cultivés par des esclaves. L'abolition de l'esclavage l'a ensuite peu à peu réduite.")},
    {"p": two("The Grays have been feuding with the Braithwaites of Braithwaite Manor, the family of [[catherine-braithwaite|Catherine Braithwaite]]. Archibald says the two families have been fighting for as long as he can remember. [[josiah-trelawny|Josiah Trelawny]] tells Dutch, in \"The New South\", that the two old plantation families have fallen out over rebel gold and over who married whom. In \"American Distillation\", Archibald says that each family believes the other stole a fortune from it long ago, and that he cannot say whether the story is true. The Red Dead Wiki dates the feud to 1806, when Lucille Braithwaite let Douglas Gray, whom the wiki counts among Tavish's ancestors, take her family's hidden gold; he used it, with gold taken from his own family, to fund abolitionist groups, and each family then accused the other of the theft. The wiki also reports that Joe Butler, a Confederate veteran in Rhodes, tells Arthur the Grays made most of their money before settling in Rhodes about fifty years earlier, and that he believes some of them spied for the Union during the war.",
              "Les Gray sont en guerre avec les Braithwaite de Braithwaite Manor, la famille de [[catherine-braithwaite|Catherine Braithwaite]] : d'aussi loin qu'Archibald s'en souvienne, les deux familles se sont toujours affrontées. Dans \"The New South\", [[josiah-trelawny|Josiah Trelawny]] explique à Dutch que les deux vieilles familles de planteurs se sont brouillées pour de l'or confédéré et des histoires de mariages entre cousins. Dans \"American Distillation\", Archibald raconte que chaque famille accuse l'autre de lui avoir volé une fortune il y a bien longtemps, sans qu'il puisse dire si l'histoire est vraie. Le Red Dead Wiki fait remonter la querelle à 1806 : Lucille Braithwaite aurait laissé Douglas Gray, que le wiki range parmi les ancêtres de Tavish, s'emparer de l'or caché de sa famille, qu'il aurait employé, avec de l'or pris aux siens, à financer des groupes abolitionnistes, chaque famille accusant ensuite l'autre du vol. Toujours d'après le wiki, Joe Butler, un ancien soldat confédéré de Rhodes, raconte à Arthur que les Gray ont fait l'essentiel de leur fortune avant de s'installer à Rhodes, une cinquantaine d'années plus tôt, et se dit convaincu que certains d'entre eux ont espionné pour le compte de l'Union pendant la guerre.")},

    # ================================================================ RDR2 1899
    {"h3": two("Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)", "Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)"), "year": "1899"},
    {"h4": two("Chapter 3: Clemens Point", "Chapitre 3 : Clemens Point"), "chapter": 3},
    {"p": two("After the move to Clemens Point, near Rhodes, [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] sends [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]] to find out about the Grays and [[hosea-matthews|Hosea Matthews]] about the Braithwaites. Arthur helps Sheriff Leigh Gray recapture the Anderson boys in \"The New South\". In \"American Distillation\", the sheriff deputizes Dutch, Arthur and [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]] to shut down a Braithwaite still. In \"The Course of True Love I\", Dutch sends Arthur to look around Caliga Hall; the guards let him in only because he says he has been deputized, and he meets Beau instead of Tavish. In \"Advertising, The New American Art\", Dutch sets out the plan: convince each family that the gang is on its side, then rob both. He also tells Arthur that [[john-marston|John Marston]] and [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] are at the Grays' place about the Braithwaites' prized horses.",
              "Une fois installé à Clemens Point, près de Rhodes, [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] charge [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]] de se renseigner sur les Gray et [[hosea-matthews|Hosea Matthews]] sur les Braithwaite. Arthur aide le shérif Leigh Gray à rattraper les frères Anderson dans \"The New South\". Dans \"American Distillation\", le shérif fait de Dutch, d'Arthur et de [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]] ses adjoints pour démanteler un alambic des Braithwaite. Dans \"The Course of True Love I\", Dutch envoie Arthur en reconnaissance à Caliga Hall ; les gardes ne le laissent entrer que parce qu'il se dit adjoint du shérif, et c'est Beau qu'il rencontre, pas Tavish. Dans \"Advertising, The New American Art\", Dutch expose son plan : persuader chaque famille que la bande est de son côté, puis les voler toutes les deux. Il apprend aussi à Arthur que [[john-marston|John Marston]] et [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] sont chez les Gray pour une affaire de chevaux de prix appartenant aux Braithwaite.")},
    {"p": two("Tavish appears in person in a single mission, \"Horse Flesh for Dinner\". Arthur joins John and Javier at the stables of Caliga Hall, where they are already talking with Tavish. Tavish is wary: he says the newcomers help everybody in town, that trouble follows them everywhere, and asks who they are. John answers that they lost money on a failed railway speculation out west. Tavish remarks that the country also suits bad men, then speaks of the war and of his family's difficulties. He blames Catherine Braithwaite and her sons for ruining the county and for killing his uncle. He says the Grays cannot be seen to get too close, and that they have gold to pay. He calls John a Yankee; John replies that his own father came over from Scotland, and Tavish says that he is Scottish too. Asked about the Braithwaites, he insults them as peasants and mongrels.",
              "Tavish n'apparaît en personne que dans une seule mission, \"Horse Flesh for Dinner\". Arthur rejoint John et Javier aux écuries de Caliga Hall, où ils discutent déjà avec Tavish. Celui-ci se méfie : ces nouveaux venus rendent service à tout le monde en ville, mais les ennuis les suivent partout, et il veut savoir qui ils sont. John prétend qu'ils ont perdu de l'argent dans l'Ouest, dans une spéculation ferroviaire ratée. Tavish fait remarquer que le pays attire aussi les mauvais garçons, puis parle de la guerre et des difficultés de sa famille. Il accuse Catherine Braithwaite et ses fils d'avoir ruiné le comté et d'avoir tué son oncle. Les Gray, dit-il, ne peuvent pas se permettre d'être vus de trop près dans cette affaire, mais ils ont de l'or pour payer. Il traite John de Yankee ; John lui répond que son propre père est arrivé d'Écosse, et Tavish rétorque qu'il est écossais lui aussi. Interrogé sur les Braithwaite, il les traite de péquenauds et de bâtards.")},
    {"p": two("Tavish then makes his offer. The Braithwaites' horses are prize animals that he values at five thousand dollars. A buyer in Clemens Cove will take them out of the state and pay half their value. He asks the three men to keep the Grays out of it in public, and tells them that the thoroughbreds are kept in the stables on the south side of the manor. John accepts. As they ride off, John calls him a crazy old fool, and Arthur says Tavish does not know what he is talking about, though a third of the price would still be worth it. At Braithwaite Manor, John tells a guard that they want to invest in the stables. A stable hand shows them the stallions Cerberus, Old Faithful and Old Father Time, and Arthur kills him. The three men take the horses and fight their way off the estate. At Clemens Cove, the fence Clay Davies says he knows the horses are not theirs and offers 650 dollars, then pays 700. Arthur writes in his journal that the gang believed a story told by one of the Grays and felt like fools (see Quotes).",
              "Tavish fait alors son offre. Les chevaux des Braithwaite sont des bêtes de prix qu'il estime à cinq mille dollars. Un acheteur de Clemens Cove les fera sortir de l'État et en paiera la moitié. Il demande aux trois hommes de tenir les Gray à l'écart de l'affaire aux yeux de tous, et leur indique que les pur-sang se trouvent dans les écuries, côté sud du manoir. John accepte. En repartant, John le traite de vieux fou, et Arthur estime que Tavish ne sait pas de quoi il parle, même si un tiers de la somme vaudrait déjà le coup. À Braithwaite Manor, John raconte à un garde qu'ils viennent investir dans les écuries. Un palefrenier leur présente les étalons Cerberus, Old Faithful et Old Father Time, puis Arthur le tue. Les trois hommes emmènent les chevaux et quittent le domaine sous les balles. À Clemens Cove, le receleur Clay Davies leur fait savoir qu'il sait que ces chevaux ne sont pas à eux, en propose 650 dollars, puis en paie 700. Dans son journal, Arthur note que la bande a cru l'histoire d'un des Gray et s'est sentie bien bête (voir Citations).")},
    {"p": two("The order in which the missions are played changes the scene. According to the Red Dead Wiki, if \"The Fine Joys of Tobacco\" has already been played, the guards at the gate tell Arthur they have had trouble, Tavish tells John and Javier that the burning of his fields makes him suspicious, and John denies any part in it, saying he prefers smoking tobacco to burning it. On the ride out, Arthur then tells John and Javier, who did not know, that he and Sean set the fire. If the horse theft comes first, Arthur warns on the ride out that Hosea and Sean, who are working the Braithwaites, had better keep their heads down. The wiki adds an optional exchange (player choice): if the player dismounts and speaks to Tavish at the start of the mission, Arthur can either thank him for the job or mock the idea that anyone would pay five thousand dollars for stolen horses.",
              "L'ordre dans lequel le joueur enchaîne les missions modifie la scène. Selon le Red Dead Wiki, si \"The Fine Joys of Tobacco\" a déjà été jouée, les gardes de l'entrée confient à Arthur qu'ils ont eu des ennuis, Tavish dit à John et Javier que l'incendie de ses champs le rend méfiant, et John nie toute implication en affirmant préférer fumer le tabac plutôt que le brûler. En repartant, Arthur révèle alors à John et Javier, qui l'ignoraient, que c'est lui qui a mis le feu avec Sean. Si le vol des chevaux vient en premier, Arthur prévient en repartant que Hosea et Sean, qui travaillent du côté des Braithwaite, ont intérêt à se faire discrets. Le wiki signale aussi un échange facultatif (au choix du joueur) : en descendant de cheval pour parler à Tavish au début de la mission, Arthur peut soit le remercier pour le travail, soit se moquer de l'idée qu'on paierait cinq mille dollars pour des chevaux volés.")},
    {"p": two("Working for Catherine Braithwaite, Arthur and [[sean-macguire|Sean MacGuire]] set fire to Tavish's tobacco fields in \"The Fine Joys of Tobacco\". On the way, Sean says he has heard that security at the estate was doubled after the trouble at the Rhodes saloon. If the horses have already been stolen, Arthur tells him that he took part, which surprises Sean. They get in by posing as a supply wagon. A guard named Hamish tells Sean that Mr. Gray has a heap of problems with another family trying to sabotage his livelihood. The guard is killed, and at nightfall Arthur and Sean douse the fields and a barn with moonshine, set them alight, fight off the guards and escape with horses from a payroll wagon.",
              "Pour le compte de Catherine Braithwaite, Arthur et [[sean-macguire|Sean MacGuire]] mettent le feu aux champs de tabac de Tavish dans \"The Fine Joys of Tobacco\". En chemin, Sean a entendu dire que la surveillance du domaine a doublé depuis l'incident du saloon de Rhodes. Si les chevaux ont déjà été volés, Arthur lui apprend qu'il était de l'expédition, à la grande surprise de Sean. Ils entrent en se faisant passer pour un chariot de ravitaillement. Un garde nommé Hamish confie à Sean que M. Gray a tout un tas d'ennuis avec une autre famille qui cherche à ruiner son affaire. Le garde est tué, puis, à la nuit tombée, Arthur et Sean arrosent d'alcool les champs et une grange, y mettent le feu, repoussent les gardes et s'enfuient avec les chevaux d'un chariot de paie.")},
    {"p": two("Tavish takes no visible part in what follows. In \"A Short Walk in a Pretty Town\", [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]] tells Arthur that some of the Grays have spoken to Bill about a security job in Rhodes. Bill says the Grays think the Braithwaites burned the fields. The job is an ambush, and Sean is shot dead in the street. Sheriff Leigh Gray tells the gang that the Grays know what it has been up to and that Rhodes is the Grays' town. He comes out of his office holding Bill hostage, with his deputies and a man named Jock (Jock Gray, a relative of Tavish, according to the Red Dead Wiki), and Arthur and Micah kill them. When Arthur gets back to camp, [[jack-marston|Jack Marston]] has been taken by the Braithwaites, and the gang burns Braithwaite Manor in \"Blood Feuds, Ancient and Modern\".",
              "Tavish ne joue aucun rôle visible dans la suite. Dans \"A Short Walk in a Pretty Town\", [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]] explique à Arthur que des membres de la famille Gray ont proposé à Bill un travail de protection à Rhodes. Bill assure que les Gray croient les Braithwaite responsables de l'incendie. Le travail est une embuscade, et Sean est abattu en pleine rue. Le shérif Leigh Gray lance à la bande que les Gray savent très bien ce qu'elle trafique et que Rhodes est la ville des Gray. Il sort de son bureau en tenant Bill en otage, avec ses adjoints et un certain Jock (Jock Gray, un parent de Tavish selon le Red Dead Wiki), et Arthur et Micah les abattent. De retour au camp, Arthur apprend que les Braithwaite ont enlevé [[jack-marston|Jack Marston]], et la bande incendie Braithwaite Manor dans \"Blood Feuds, Ancient and Modern\".")},

    # ================================================================ Death
    {"h3": two("Death and the letter from Edinburgh", "Sa mort et la lettre d'Édimbourg"), "year": ""},
    {"p": two("The game never shows Tavish's death and never states its cause. Arthur can come across him on a porch of the main house (the back porch, according to the Red Dead Wiki), at a point of interest called \"Gray's Secret\". Tavish is slumped forward in a wicker chair, his right hand on his left forearm. Beside him stands a small marble table with a metal pot and a cup. No weapon or wound is visible. The Red Dead Wiki's page on the point of interest says the body can be found once \"Horse Flesh for Dinner\" is completed, while the wiki's page on Tavish places his death some time after the Rhodes ambush.",
              "Le jeu ne montre jamais la mort de Tavish et n'en donne jamais la cause. Arthur peut le découvrir sous un porche de la maison principale (celui de l'arrière, d'après le Red Dead Wiki), au point d'intérêt baptisé \"Gray's Secret\". Tavish est assis, affaissé vers l'avant dans un fauteuil en osier, la main droite posée sur l'avant-bras gauche. À côté de lui, un petit guéridon en marbre porte un pot en métal et une tasse. Aucune arme ni aucune blessure n'est visible. La page du Red Dead Wiki consacrée au point d'intérêt indique que le corps est accessible dès la fin de \"Horse Flesh for Dinner\", tandis que la page du wiki sur Tavish situe sa mort quelque temps après l'embuscade de Rhodes.")},
    {"p": two("A letter lies on the table beside him. It is dated April 3, 1895, comes from Malcolm Moffat, senior professor of history at Edinburgh University, and is addressed to \"Mr. Gray\". Moffat thanks him for his \"long and well researched letter\" about an ancestor who left Scotland for the colonies after the Jacobite rising of 1745, and admits he could not tell whether the man was his great-grandfather or great-great-grandfather. He writes that he is sorry to disappoint a man so proud of being a Scot living in exile, as his correspondent describes himself (see Names).",
              "Une lettre est posée sur le guéridon, à côté de lui. Datée du 3 avril 1895, elle émane de Malcolm Moffat, professeur principal d'histoire à l'université d'Édimbourg, et s'adresse à \"Mr. Gray\". Moffat le remercie pour sa longue lettre bien documentée sur un ancêtre qui a quitté l'Écosse pour les colonies après le soulèvement jacobite de 1745, et avoue ne pas avoir compris s'il s'agissait de son arrière-grand-père ou de son arrière-arrière-grand-père. Il regrette de devoir décevoir un homme si fier de se dire Écossais en exil (voir Noms).")},
    {"p": two("Moffat has studied the spy networks of the Duke of Cumberland, who kept precise records. According to those records, the ancestor, Ross Gray, was \"unquestionably a well-paid informer\". He was paid in cattle and cash and was given land confiscated from his neighbor. Moffat writes that this explains why Ross Gray stayed in Scotland until 1755, ten years after the rising, the year some Jacobite supporters began reprisals against known informers in the Highlands. Moffat adds that his own ancestors include both rebels and loyalists, that descending from loyalists is nothing to be ashamed of, and invites Mr. Gray to visit the university. Arthur and John each write about the discovery in their journals (see Quotes).",
              "Moffat a étudié les réseaux d'espions du duc de Cumberland, qui tenait ses archives avec précision. D'après ces archives, l'ancêtre en question, Ross Gray, était sans le moindre doute un informateur grassement payé. Il a été rétribué en bétail et en argent, et a reçu des terres confisquées à son voisin. C'est ce qui explique, selon Moffat, que Ross Gray ne soit parti d'Écosse qu'en 1755, dix ans après le soulèvement, l'année où quelques partisans jacobites ont commencé à se venger des informateurs connus dans les Highlands. Moffat précise que ses propres ancêtres comptent à la fois des rebelles et des loyalistes, qu'il n'y a aucune honte à descendre de loyalistes, et invite son correspondant à venir visiter l'université. Arthur comme John consignent la découverte dans leur journal (voir Citations).")},

    # ================================================================ 1907
    {"h3": two("Red Dead Redemption 2: the epilogue (1907)", "Red Dead Redemption 2 : l'épilogue (1907)"), "year": "1907"},
    {"p": two("According to the Red Dead Wiki, Tavish's body is still in its chair in 1907, unchanged and untouched, when John can visit Caliga Hall. The same source says the Grays have kept Caliga Hall: its tobacco is still farmed by day and armed men still guard it by night. In Rhodes, according to the wiki, Sheriff Harmon Thomas was elected after Leigh Gray's death on a promise to free the town from both families. In \"A Quick Favor for an Old Friend\", [[sadie-adler|Sadie Adler]] tells John that the sheriff has done a lot to bring Rhodes into line since the time of the Grays and the Braithwaites. According to the quote list of the Red Dead Wiki, [[simon-pearson|Simon Pearson]], who now runs the general store in Rhodes, tells John that people in town still talk about the brutal end of both families.",
              "Selon le Red Dead Wiki, le corps de Tavish est toujours dans son fauteuil en 1907, intact et sans que personne n'y ait touché, quand John peut se rendre à Caliga Hall. Toujours selon le wiki, Caliga Hall reste aux mains des Gray : le tabac y est cultivé le jour, et des hommes armés le gardent la nuit. À Rhodes, d'après la même source, le shérif Harmon Thomas a été élu après la mort de Leigh Gray en promettant d'affranchir la ville des deux familles. Dans \"A Quick Favor for an Old Friend\", [[sadie-adler|Sadie Adler]] confie à John que le shérif a beaucoup fait pour remettre de l'ordre à Rhodes depuis l'époque des Gray et des Braithwaite. D'après la liste de citations du Red Dead Wiki, [[simon-pearson|Simon Pearson]], qui tient désormais le magasin général de Rhodes, raconte à John qu'on parle encore en ville de la fin brutale des deux familles.")},
]
